{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SFdJ7LGWpGYkHrcNpT6eDw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand what needs to be done.\n\n## Project State Summary\n\nThis is a Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils/moreutils, verified via differential testing. The project uses a specification-driven pipeline where specs are written first, then code is generated by an AI orchestrator.\n\n## Current State\n\nLooking at the `requirement_states` field, I can see which requirements are in \"ready\" state:\n\n**srd004-ts:**\n- R9.2: ready\n\n\n- R10.1: ready\n- R10.2: ready\n- R10.3: ready\n\n**srd105-stty:**\n- R7.2: ready\n- R7.3: ready\n\n**srd110-pr:**\n- R2.1: ready\n- R2.2: ready\n- R2.3: ready\n- R3.1: ready\n- R4.1: ready\n- R4.2: ready\n- R4.3: ready\n- R5.1: ready\n- R5.2: ready\n\n**srd111-ptx:**\n- R2.1: ready\n- R2.2: ready\n- R2.3: ready\n- R3.1: ready\n- R4.1: ready\n- R4.2: ready\n- R5.1: ready\n- R5.2: ready\n\nAll four services map to release 15.0 and fall within the allowed scope. Now I'm checking the code status for each release component to see what's been started.\n\nLooking across earlier releases, I'm finding several use cases still marked as not started across versions 00.0 through 04.1, so I need to scan through the full list to identify all the incomplete items. I'm seeing a lot of test cases across multiple releases that haven't been started yet, but there's an important constraint I need to apply: I should only propose tasks for requirements marked as \"ready\" in the requirement_states field. Since that field only lists a specific subset of requirements, I need to filter my focus to just those ready items rather than tackling everything on this backlog. I need to figure out the weight assignments for these requirements, but I don't have direct access to the requirements.yaml file. The context hints that release 15.0 restructured