he stty command with requirements R7.2 and R7.3 from the SRD, following the same pattern of modifying the main implementation and extending the differential test suite. text: \"go vet ./cmd/stty/ reports no issues\"\n\nMoving on to the next task, I need to implement several requirements for the ts command tool, specifically R9.2 and R10.1 through R10.3 from the SRD. I'll be extending the existing implementation in cmd/ts/main.go and adding differential test cases to cmd/ts/ts_test.go using the same testing framework. R9.2, R10.1, R10.2, R10.3\n\nrequirements:\n  - id: R1\n    text: \"Implement srd004-ts requirement R9.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n  - id: R2\n    text: \"Implement srd004-ts requirement R10.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n  - id: R3\n    text: \"Implement srd004-ts requirement R10.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n  - id: R4\n    text: \"Implement srd004-ts requirement R10.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n\ndesign_decisions:\n  - id: D1\n    text: \"Follow existing patterns in cmd/ts/main.go for new functionality\"\n  - id: D2\n    text: \"Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests for all differential test cases\"\n  - id: D3\n    text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environments per project convention\"\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    text: \"All four requirements (R9.2, R10.1, R10.2, R10.3) implemented per SRD acceptance criteria\"\n  - id: AC2\n    text: \"go build ./cmd/ts/ succeeds with no errors\"\n  - id: AC3\n    text: \"go test ./cmd/ts/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if reference binary not found)\"\n  - id: AC4\n    text: \"go vet ./cmd/ts/ reports no issues\"\n\nI should also review pkg/sys/ where relevant since the ts utility handles timestamps on stdin, and stty deals with terminal settings which definitely uses sys. I need to check the component dependencies to see what's already documented there.\n\nLooking at the architecture, I don't see explicit entries for ts, stty, pr, or ptx, but the SRD will specify their dependencies. The stitch agent will