{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SFdJ7LGWpGYkHrcNpT6eDw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge in edge-case behavior. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI orchestrator, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/` provides shared infrastructure (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), `docs/specs/` holds SRDs as the source of truth, and `magefiles/` drives the build/generation pipeline.\n\n**Implementation state:** Generation run 44 is active on `generation-run44`. Most releases (00.0 through 14.0) have partial to full implementation across ~111 utilities. Release 15.0 (complex utilities: ts, stty, pr, ptx) is in progress -- ts has active commits through R9.1, other three have earlier requirements completed.\n\n**Current release:** 15.0. Four utilities remain with \"ready\" requirements:\n- **ts** (srd004): R9.2, R10.1, R10.2, R10.3\n- **stty** (srd105): R7.2, R7.3\n- **pr** (srd110): R2.1-R2.3, R3.1, R4.1-R4.3, R5.1-R5.2\n- **ptx** (srd111): R2.1-R2.3, R3.1, R4.1-R4.2, R5.1-R5.2\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nAll ready requirements are in release 15.0. Within the release, canonical ordering applies (alphabetical by file path): pr, ptx, stty, ts. All four packages already have earlier requirements completed, so no contract tasks are needed.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAll requirement groups with multiple sub-requirements (R2.x, R4.x, R5.x, R7.x, R9.x, R10.x) are assumed weight 1 each. Standalone group requirements (R3.1 in pr and ptx) are potentially weight 4 per the release 15.0 restructuring note (\"each weight-4 requirement is in its own group\"). To stay safe, R3.1 is excluded from multi-requirement tasks.\n\n```\nTask 0: srd110-pr R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd111-ptx R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd105-stty R7.2 (w=1), R7.3 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1 = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd004-ts R9.2 (w=1), R10.1 (w=1), R10.2 (w=1), R10.3 (w=1)\n  Total weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\nRemaining for future batch: pr R3.1, R4.1-R4.3, R5.1-R5.2; ptx R3.1, R4.1-R4.2, R5.1-R5.2.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/pr implementation (srd110-pr R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.yaml (requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/pr/main.go (existing implementation to extend)\n      - cmd/pr/pr_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (RunDiffTests differential testing framework)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/pr/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Implement srd110-pr R2.1, R2.2, R2.3\n      - path: cmd/pr/pr_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R2.1, R2.2, R2.3\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd110-pr requirement R2.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd110-pr requirement R2.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd110-pr requirement R2.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow existing patterns in cmd/pr/main.go for new functionality\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests for all differential test cases\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environments per project convention\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"Requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 implemented per SRD